	(label "VBUS"
		(at 114.3 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e62e739e-e08b-5336-9443-02493967fb1b")
	)
	(text "BreadPortZero: I2C x4 (STEMMA QT/Qwiic + 0.1 in sockets), SPI, UART and 4 analog inputs for the CardputerZero top port, with a USB-C supplemental 5 V input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "80b0e06d-d015-5dde-9418-1437d69b58d2")
	)
	(text "J1 pin map from M5Stack's port photo: 12 = G14 TX, 14 = G15 RX (the docs table swaps them)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 259.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8817dae0-a598-571c-ad65-40d0e597b5e3")
	)
	(text "Power: 5VOUT (pin 6, Settings > ExtPort) -> U1 TPS2553 (234-303 mA, R1 = 100k) -> D3 -> +5V_SW -> U2 TLV62569 buck -> 3.3 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d0e0b048-e930-5633-8056-f90c23bb471d")
	)
	(text "USB-C J13 (5.1k Rd on CC) -> D4 TVS -> U6 TPS2553 (1.09-1.26 A, R24 = 22k) -> +5V_SW. U6 shares U1's EN, so USB only powers the cap while the host's 5VOUT is on; D3 makes USB (higher) carry the load and blocks it from the host"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 269.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1fae196a-6216-5ec4-b65d-5dc0ce49dd63")
	)
	(text "Neither source can back-feed the other: D3 blocks USB from the host's 5V, U6 blocks the host from VBUS (1 uA max reverse with VIN = 0). D2 lights while U1 (host path) limits current or is in thermal shutdown (U6's FAULT is left open)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 274.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "be19a482-fc95-55db-b6b0-f55b75dfa0be")
	)
	(text "SPI: G11/G10/G9 are shared with the CardputerZero's display (CE0), so U7 (74LVC125) buffers them. MISO drives G9 only while CS (G7) is low; Ioff isolates the display's bus when the cap is off. D5-D8: socket ESD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 279.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0ec702aa-5a06-52da-8a6f-f8c3de22d5a0")
	)
	(text "Power switch: R15 holds EN (U1, U6, U2) high. Bridge JP9 and drive G7 high to turn BreadPortZero off (Q3 pulls EN low); R16 keeps it on while G7 floats or carries the Pi's default pull-up. JP9 bridged = no SPI CS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 284.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "de1304bf-18b2-5fa4-9579-c6e02160b288")
	)
	(text "External I2C bus on G22 (SDA) / G23 (SCL), a software bus (dtoverlay=i2c-gpio) apart from the host's I2C1 (keyboard, RTC, IMU). Bridge JP1 + JP2 to put it on I2C1 instead"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 289.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d30bb4ab-c8b1-56dc-96f0-87ae36e93761")
	)
	(text "Q1/Q2: I2C isolation, gates on BreadPortZero's 3.3 V; unpowered, the external bus is cut off from the host. R12/R13: host-side pull-ups (cut JP8 if JP1/JP2 are bridged). U4: ESD protection. JP3: cut to remove the 4.7k pull-ups"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 294.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "697117f9-08f2-54f7-87f3-c74a2ab4bc75")
	)
	(text "U3 ADS1115: JP4 1-2 (as made) = 0x48, 2-3 = 0x49; cut JP4 and bridge JP6 = 0x4A or JP5 = 0x4B. JP7: bridge to bring ALERT/RDY to G26"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 299.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "981b8060-7cc0-5f55-8ccd-53d88b4d9eb9")
	)
	(text "Analog inputs 0-3.3 V: R5-R8 with C5-C8 = 1.6 kHz anti-alias filter, and they limit fault current. R17-R20 (not fitted): divider pads, e.g. 1.8k for 0-5 V inputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 304.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ee59bb9f-f130-527d-a4a7-e3405e8d5c0c")
	)
	(text "R10/R11 (4.7k) limit current into or out of a UART device that is unpowered or runs at 5 V. U5: ESD protection on the UART socket"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 309.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0712d546-deaf-55d0-8325-5f0ed35a53d0")
	)
